      "token_count": null,
      "status": "200 OK",
      "player_input": "Josie",
      "ai_response": "The air hangs thick with the scent of ozone and dust, a sharp contrast to the lingering memory of your old world. Shouts echo from the street outside, muffled by stone but insistent, punctuated by the distant rumble of something heavy. The space you stand in, designated as the \"Entry,\" is relatively intact, though a fine layer of grit coats everything, and a spiderweb of cracks mars the flagstone floor. To your left, a stout wooden door, its varnish chipped and dull, leads into what the map indicates is the Foyer. The light filtering in from the street is weak, casting long, dancing shadows that do little to ease the tension coiling in your gut.\n\n1. Examine the cracks on the floor more closely.\n2. Try the stout wooden door leading to the Foyer.\n3. Call out a greeting into the Entry.\n4. Step back outside to see what's happening in the street.\n\nWhat do you do?",
      "error_stack": null,
      "save_id": "22a4f976-fc6f-467c-9af7-6927eaefd5d5"
